      "problem": "Find $|z|$ if $z=-2k+5t\\text{i},$ where $k$ and $t$ are real numbers.",
      "worked_solution": "For a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=-2k+5t\\text{i},$ we have $a=-2k$ and $b=5t.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|-2k+5t\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{(-2k)^{2}+(5t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+25{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
